==Services==
===The "Spirit of Okaiken" Cabin===
[[File:Sanesair Spirit of Okaiken - First Square.png|thumb|Sanesair "Spirit of Okaiken" flagship First Class suite on the Airbus A350-1000.]]
[[File:Sanesair Spirit of Okaiken - Business Class.png|thumb|Sanesair "Spirit of Okaiken" Business Class on the Airbus A350-1000.]]
[[File:Sanesair Spirit of Okaiken - Premium Economy.png|thumb|Sanesair "Spirit of Okaiken" Premium Economy Class on the Airbus A350-1000.]]
[[File:Sanesair Spirit of Okaiken - Economy.png|thumb|Sanesair "Spirit of Okaiken" Economy Class on the Airbus A350-1000.]]

Introduced in 2025 to coincide with the 15th Anniversary of the [[Jutsu Restoration]], the "Spirit of Okaiken" cabin represents the pinnacle of "Technocratic Hospitality". The concept features fully enclosed "High Ground" suites in First Class, staggered fully-flat beds in Diamond Business, and ergonomically optimized fixed-shell seats in the Ordinary (Economy) cabins. A central feature of the new interior is the Avatar in-flight entertainment system, developed in partnership with [[Kizan Systems]]. This platform utilizes the Satori AI to provide predictive meal ordering, personalized cabin lighting based on passenger biometrics, and seamless high-speed connectivity via the Satori Sky-Sync satellite network.

In line with the national rebranding, Sanesair discontinued its legacy "Club Sankei" business class branding, consolidating its premium services under the Diamond Business and Imperial First banners. The airline also overhauled its ground experience, opening the flagship Sanesair Crimson Lounge at Okami-Tobu International and the Mican Lounge for domestic regional hubs like Mito and Waseda.

[[File:Sanesair Cabin Lighting.jpg|thumb|Satori-integrated "Smart Cabin" lighting on a Sanesair Boeing 787-9.]]

The "Spirit of Okaiken" concept was originally intended to debut in late 2024 with the delivery of the first refurbished Boeing 787-9s. however, the rollout faced significant delays due to the failure of safety certification for new seat-frame components. This forced the debut back to April 2025, when it finally launched on the flagship Okami-Tobu to [[Balisca]] route.

Following the success of the initial launch, the airline initiated the Project Komorebi refurbishment program. This initiative saw the high-tech interior refitted across the existing long-haul fleet, including the Boeing 787 Dreamliners and the newer Airbus A350-900 units. The refurbished A350-900s notably debuted the boutique 1-1-1 First Class suite layout, which has since become the industry standard for trans-Fosian corridors.

Reflecting the piquant culinary preferences of the Sanese people, all "Spirit of Okaiken" cabins feature the Spiceworks dining program. Premium passengers enjoy multi-course ''Kaiseki'' meals from the "Taste of the Three Islands" menu, prepared using high-altitude induction heating technology to preserve the aggressive heat of Sanese chili peppers. Since 2014, all international long-haul aircraft have been equipped with Satori-integrated "Smart Lavatories," featuring automated sanitization cycles and, on the Boeing 787 and A350 fleets, signature Sanese bidets in all classes.

